---
/**
 * PARENT PARTNERSHIP · PARENTS' FORUM — audit §2F.
 *
 * ⚠ REBUILT. The previous version passed the parent section's own <Forum />
 * component into TopicPage — literally the same component the overview composes,
 * shown twice. This page now carries what only it can: the school's own agenda,
 * transcribed off its own projected slide, and the class nameplates on its own
 * desks. Neither appears anywhere else on the site.
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE — read off the school's own published photographs ══════════════
 *   assets/parents forum/parents forum (5).jpg — the agenda, projected and
 *   legible, headed "Agenda for Parents Forum: Session 2025-26 Class IX to XII)"
 *   and running to twelve numbered items:
 *     1 Almanac · 2 Syllabi · 3 Quality of classroom teaching · 4 Pace of
 *     teaching · 5 Quality of assignment in Learner's Comate / Class work /
 *     Homework · 6 Question Bank · 7 E-Portfolio · 8 Grandparents Cove ·
 *     9 Positive Affirmations · 10 Scientific Facts · 11 Correction of
 *     Notebooks / Learner's Comate · 12 Fruit Break
 *   The same frame shows a panel of four staff behind a name plate reading
 *   Dr. Arpita Singh — the school's principal.
 *
 *   assets/parents forum/parents forum (3).jpg — every desk carries a class
 *   nameplate: Nursery, KG-I A, II-C, II-E, III-A. A parent sits FOR a named
 *   class, which makes the forum a representative body rather than an open
 *   meeting. That sitting is a junior one; the projected agenda above is from a
 *   Classes IX–XII sitting, so the school runs the forum more than once.
 *
 * ⚠ "LEARNER'S COMATE" IS TRANSCRIBED, NOT EXPANDED. It is the school's own
 * spelling on its own slide. What the artefact is — a diary, a workbook, a
 * portfolio — is not published, so it is quoted and left alone.
 *
 * ⚠ A NAME DISCREPANCY WORTH THE CLIENT'S ATTENTION: data/site.ts records the
 * principal as "Mrs. Arpita Singh"; her own name plate in this photograph reads
 * "Dr. Arpita Singh". This page says "the principal" and names no honorific.
 *
 * ⚠ NOT CLAIMED: how often the forum sits, how a representative is chosen, how
 * long a term runs, or what was decided at any session.
 *
 * Composition: split (paper, photo RIGHT — the room) → collage (sand, LEFT —
 * the agenda, all twelve items, grouped and quoted) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcSplit from '../../../components/academics/system/AcSplit.astro';
import AcCollage from '../../../components/academics/system/AcCollage.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/parents forum/parents forum (5).jpg';
import pSeats from '../../../assets/parents forum/parents forum (3).jpg';
import pPanel from '../../../assets/parents forum/parents forum (5).jpg';
import pRows from '../../../assets/parents forum/parents forum (2).jpg';
import pCohort from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-3.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Parents’ Forum — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="The Parents' Forum at Sunbeam School Ballia: a seat per class section, a leadership panel, and a twelve-item agenda covering teaching quality, pace, homework and the correction of notebooks."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Parents’ Forum"
    standfirst="A seat with your child’s class written on it, and an agenda projected on the wall."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
      { label: 'Parent Partnership', href: '/academics/parent-partnership/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="The leadership panel at a Parents' Forum session at Sunbeam School Ballia, the session's agenda projected on the screen beside them."
    position="50% 46%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcSplit
      ground="paper"
      side="right"
      ratio="wide"
      aspect="3 / 2"
      kicker="Not a parent–teacher meeting"
      heading="A seat with<br /><em>a class on it</em>"
      body={[
        'The clearest thing about Sunbeam’s forum is visible on the furniture. Every desk in the room carries a class nameplate — <strong>Nursery, KG-I A, II-C, II-E, III-A</strong> — so a parent is not attending in general. They are sitting <em>for</em> a class, and what they raise is raised on that class’s behalf.',
        'That is what separates the forum from a parent–teacher meeting. A PTM is about one child, with that child’s teachers, in private. The forum is about the school, with the school’s leadership, in front of the other parents — and the answer is given to the room.',
        'It sits more than once: the room above is a junior session, while the agenda in the next section was projected at a sitting for <strong>Classes IX to XII</strong>.',
      ]}
      photo={pSeats}
      alt={`Parents of ${school} seated at desks in the forum room, each desk carrying a class nameplate — Nursery, KG-I A, II-C, II-E and III-A`}
      inset={pRows}
      insetAlt={`Parents of ${school} seated in the tiered rows of the hall during a Parents’ Forum session`}
    />

    <AcCollage
      ground="sand"
      side="left"
      kicker="Session 2025-26 · Classes IX to XII"
      heading="Twelve items,<br /><em>on the wall</em>"
      body={[
        'The school projects the agenda rather than keeping it at the front table, which means every parent in the room can see the whole list — including the items still to come. All twelve are below, in the school’s own words, grouped only for reading.',
        'Four of them are the questions parents most often have no formal channel for: <em>quality of classroom teaching</em>, <em>pace of teaching</em>, <em>quality of assignment</em>, and <em>correction of notebooks</em>. Those are on a published agenda here, not raised as a complaint.',
      ]}
      ledger={[
        { k: 'The teaching itself', v: '“Quality of classroom teaching” · “Pace of teaching”.' },
        { k: 'The work that comes home', v: '“Quality of assignment in Learner’s Comate / Class work / Homework” · “Correction of Notebooks / Learner’s Comate”.' },
        { k: 'The documents', v: '“Almanac” · “Syllabi” · “Question Bank” · “E-Portfolio”.' },
        { k: 'And the rest of the child', v: '“Grandparents Cove” · “Positive Affirmations” · “Scientific Facts” · “Fruit Break”.' },
      ]}
      lead={{ src: pPanel, alt: `The leadership panel at a Parents’ Forum session at ${school}, the twelve-item agenda projected on the screen beside them` }}
      support={[
        { src: pRows, alt: `Parents of ${school} seated in the tiered rows of the hall during a Parents’ Forum session` },
        { src: pSeats, alt: `Desks at a Parents’ Forum session at ${school}, each carrying a class nameplate` },
      ]}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Answered<br /><em>to the room.</em>"
      body="The school publishes the forum, its agenda and the classes each sitting covers. How often it sits, how a class representative is chosen, and what was decided at any session are not published."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Students and staff of ${school} gathered on the hall stage`}
      position="50% 42%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
